# CODEOWNERS — Smatchet sensitive-path review map.
#
# Format: <pattern> <owner>... — patterns follow .gitignore semantics, later
# entries override earlier matches for the same path. See:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-customization/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Today @alexandrosk0 is the sole owner. CODEOWNERS is INFORMATIONAL until
# branch protection is reconfigured to require code-owner review — the file
# documents what the project considers sensitive and gives a single edit
# point when additional owners are added.
#
# Phase 7a of docs/design/git-ref-plan-locks.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Plan-lock coordination infrastructure (git-ref-plan-locks)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The primitive scripts + helpers that touch refs/locks/* on origin live in the
# agent layer (the agent-layer/ submodule, the-unwilling-agentic-bunch), whose
# own CODEOWNERS covers them. Here a change to them arrives as a pointer bump of
# the gitlink, so the mount itself is the sensitive path. A malicious or buggy
# edit there can race-corrupt any in-flight slice's claim.
/agent-layer                           @alexandrosk0
/.gitmodules                           @alexandrosk0

# Workflows that hold delete-ref + open-issue + open-PR privileges with the
# default GITHUB_TOKEN. Self-modification risk: a PR could edit the workflow
# itself to broaden its blast radius.
.github/workflows/locks-render.yml     @alexandrosk0
.github/workflows/lock-cleanup.yml     @alexandrosk0
.github/workflows/lock-staleness.yml   @alexandrosk0

# Plan-lock design + historical archive. Plan doc is the spec; archive is
# the audit trail of every lock that ever existed pre-cutover.
docs/design/git-ref-plan-locks.md      @alexandrosk0
docs/design/_plan-locks-archive.md     @alexandrosk0

# CODEOWNERS itself — modifying ownership requires owner approval (once
# branch-protection enforces this rule).
/.github/CODEOWNERS                    @alexandrosk0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-target invariants
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build system — touching CMake / preset config affects every downstream
# build target and the dual-target Standalone + Unreal contract.
/CMakeLists.txt                        @alexandrosk0
/CMakePresets.json                     @alexandrosk0
/cmake/                                @alexandrosk0

# Public C++ contracts whose ABI surface is consumed by both targets and
# every tracker backend / command system / Lua binding.
Source/Core/include/ITracker*.h        @alexandrosk0
Source/Core/include/Commands/          @alexandrosk0

# Top-level agent entry point. AGENTS.md is the stub that imports the layer's
# rulebook (agent-layer/AGENTS.md); CLAUDE.md is Claude Code's auto-load path.
/AGENTS.md                             @alexandrosk0
/.claude/CLAUDE.md                     @alexandrosk0
